# Who has to look at a change before it lands.
#
# There is one maintainer, so this file looks redundant. It is here so the
# request survives the lab growing: a security-sensitive path in a repository
# with no owner is a path nobody reads, and the default answer should be a
# person rather than whoever happened to open the pull request.
#
# The paths are chosen so that the things which can end a process, sign a
# release, handle a key or make a network call cannot be changed by anyone who
# has not been through this repository before.

